    "caul": {
      "word": "CAUL",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "A covering of network for the head, worn by women; also, a net. Spenser.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Anat.)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The fold of membrane loaded with fat, which covers more or less of the intestines in mammals; the great omentum See Omentum. The caul serves for warming of the lower belly. Ray.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "A part of the amnion, one of the membranes enveloping the fetus, which sometimes is round the head of a child at its birth. It is deemed lucky to be with a caul or membrane over the face. This caul is esteemed an infallible preservative against drowning . . . According to Chysostom, the midwives frequently sold it for magic uses. Grose. I was born with a caul, which was advertised for sale, in the newspapers, at the low price of fifteen guineas. Dickens.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
      "relatedWords": []
    },
